    "notes": "Headless command lane, 13 boots, no display and no debugger, CORROBORATED on the live-session channel by three further runs (two workers, two different incoming tools, the item-mode preset rather than the raw rotate tool, and the Y axis rather than X): all four agree that press 1 leaves the edit standing and press 2 removes it. The rotation AXIS differs by rig and is NOT part of the law -- the symbols block holds each side's own literal and the law is the TRAJECTORY. The observable is the item's rotation CHANNEL, never vertex positions: an item transform does not move mesh points, so a vertex read is byte-identical under every candidate. WHAT THIS FIXTURE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT PIN: the DROP door. Headless it reads the same trajectory as the switch; live it clears at press 1 instead of press 2, and the live reading is the one to believe because the coalescing machinery is a UI-side session the headless lane never opens. A drop-door row would have frozen a channel artefact as a law. Task 4520 owns it."
